menu "Moonwater Canvas"
    config MOONWATER_CANVAS
        bool "Moonwater Canvas, the kernel's side of the desktop"
        depends on MOONWATER_CORE=y && DRM && DRM_CLIENT
        default y
        help
          Own the display from kernel space until the desktop starts:
          Canvas claims each card as an in-kernel DRM client, chooses the
          mode and the scale, commits a first picture and holds the card
          until the compositor, a program, takes it as DRM master. When the
          compositor lets go of the card Canvas draws the ground again.
          Its source is src/canvas/, an object of its own beside the core,
          which is why the core has to be built in. Disable this option to
          omit it and the architecture-specific pixel assembly entirely;
          Moonwater core, Spark programs and the ordinary kernel consoles
          remain available.

    config MOONWATER_CANVAS_AUTOSTART
        bool "Start Canvas automatically during boot"
        depends on MOONWATER_CANVAS && MOONWATER_SHELL
        default y
        help
          Probe DRM devices and claim them as soon as display drivers
          appear, so the machine script can start the compositor.

          Disable this while keeping MOONWATER_CANVAS enabled to retain the
          compositor in the image without claiming a display at boot. The
          ordinary framebuffer, virtual or serial console then owns /dev/console
          and PID 1 starts the shell directly on it. Ensure the kernel command
          line does not contain drm_client_lib.active=, which intentionally
          suppresses the framebuffer console for a Canvas-first desktop.

endmenu # Moonwater Canvas
